{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Findings 2/3 — contract evaluation per candidate (AC3, AC4)\n\nKey structural result: all three candidates change **only the `needs_folding` trigger predicate** (WHEN to fold). They do **not** touch snapshot placement (`build_snapshot_event`'s gap-timestamp between newest-folded and youngest-live), `source_event_uuids` computation, the `*.retired` retire/restore rule, `.snapshot-rebuild.bak` crash sentinel, or replay ordering (`reducer/_replay.py` HLC sort). The ADR-0035 invariants live in those unchanged paths, so they hold for every candidate.\n\n| Contract (source) | A fixed (control) | B geometric | C byte-cost | Why |\n|---|:--:|:--:|:--:|---|\n| Conservative fold horizon — hot-edge (`< COMPACTION_HORIZON_NS`) stays live, snapshot gap-timestamped (ADR 0035 Opt 3) | PASS | PASS | PASS | horizon partitions WHICH events fold; cadence only gates WHEN. `foldable` is still computed after the horizon cut in all candidates. |\n| Rebuild-on-stray (fsck `rebuild_snapshot_from_full_log`, ADR 0035 Opt 1) | PASS | PASS | PASS | rebuild recomputes from the full ordered log incl. `*.retired`, bypassing cache; independent of how often normal folds fire. |\n| Crash recovery (`compact_txn` atomic retire/restore + `.snapshot-rebuild.bak`) | PASS | PASS | PASS | atomicity is per-fold and cadence-agnostic; fewer folds = fewer crash windows, never more. |\n| Mixed-version rollback | PASS | PASS | PASS | snapshots are self-describing envelopes; an old binary (fixed T=10) reads a new-cadence store and vice-versa — no format change. Default-off config (below) makes rollback a pure no-op. |\n| Two-clone merge-as-union convergence | PASS | PASS | PASS* | cadence is a pure function of locally-visible state; divergent fold points across clones are already normal for fixed-count and are absorbed by union + gap-timestamp + rebuild-on-stray. *Requires the pre-implementation two-clone reconvergence test (see assumptions). |\n\n**Read-cost (replay) is the real trade between candidates, not a contract failure.** The control keeps replay trivially small (≤16 events) but pays Θ(N²) storage. Pure geometric keeps storage linear but lets the replay tail grow to ~N/2 events (2,880 @ N=8,000) — unbounded in absolute terms. Byte-cost bounds the replayed **bytes** to α·(snapshot bytes): reading the live tail then costs at most a fraction α of loading the snapshot itself, so total read cost stays within a constant factor (1+α) of the unavoidable snapshot load — the correct invariant for a growing state."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787569354964885001,"uuid":"ebdf9122-f844-4e9c-bfd0-c0f3fa58856f"}